# fshelper_imports.lnk - wlink import directives for the kernel file system
# helper calls (module FSHELPER) used by HFS/2.
#
# GPL v2 or later.  Clean-room, written 2026 from public sources; see
# PROVENANCE2.md.
#
# Use:   wlink @hfs.lnk      with a line   @fshelper_imports.lnk   in hfs.lnk
#        (wlink accepts "@file" inside a directive file), for example:
#
#            system os2 dll
#            name hfs.ifs
#            file ...your objects...
#            @fshelper_imports.lnk
#
# How the kernel exports them: the helpers are NOT in a disk DLL.  They are
# entries of the kernel-provided module named FSHELPER, and the IFS imports
# them by ORDINAL (the module has no usable names).  Ordinals and module name
# were confirmed in two independent public sources (see PROVENANCE2.md).
#
# Syntax (Open Watcom linker guide, IMPORT directive):
#       IMPORT internal_name module_name.ordinal
# internal_name is the symbol the object files reference.  For a function
# declared `far pascal` Open Watcom 16-bit emits the name in UPPER CASE with
# no underscore (predefined __pascal alias), which is exactly what is written
# below.  If you declare the helpers with another convention the linker will
# report unresolved externals; adjust the internal names then (a quick check:
# wdis the object, or read the unresolved list of the first link).
#
# Only the helpers HFS/2 calls are active.  The others of the module are
# listed commented out for completeness (all 55 entries of the table).
#
# Alternative: build an import library once and link it instead:
#     wlib -b -n fshelper.lib ++FSH_SEMCLEAR.FSHELPER..FSH_SEMCLEAR.7 ...
# (wlib entry syntax: ++sym.dll_name[.[altsym].export_name][.ordinal]).
# The exact wlib spelling for "ordinal only" is UNVERIFIED (not run here: no
# Open Watcom on this machine); the IMPORT lines below are the primary route.

# --- used by HFS/2 (37) -----------------------------------------------------
import FSH_SEGALLOC           FSHELPER.1
import FSH_SEGFREE            FSHELPER.2
import FSH_SEGREALLOC         FSHELPER.3
import FSH_FORCENOSWAP        FSHELPER.4
